 "schema_version": 1,
 "name": "CDMS ELIT (Gated)",
 "notes": "REFERENCE: trap design and dimensions from J. A. Hogan & M. F. Jarrold, 'Optimized Electrostatic Linear Ion Trap for Charge Detection Mass Spectrometry', J. Am. Soc. Mass Spectrom. 29, 2086-2095 (2018), DOI 10.1007/s13361-018-2007-x (the cylindrical trap); voltages and beamline from 's slide (2026-08-12). MEASURED (2026-08-12, v334, 3 ms flights): 12/12 TRAPPED at both a pinned (11) and a random seed, 10 oscillations each at the ELIT period. 's inj_85V 85 -> 105 V retune is credited: ions cross that 52.6 mm element at 20 eV instead of 40, the gentler acceleration lowers the divergence at the 0.94 mm exit aperture, and the whole ensemble lands inside the trap's radial acceptance (the previous tune captured 4/12, losing the rest on the 1.65 mm shield bore). Trapping is classified by BEHAVIOR (>= 2 tube-center crossings and staying inside), not endpoint position: a mono-energetic tob-locked ensemble is phase-locked, and t_max catches all ions together at the entrance-mirror turning point (x ~ 222), which an endpoint-window test misreads as lost. TAU RE-MEASURED 578.0 us (2026-08-12) after 's column retune (inj_85V 85 -> 105 V): ions cross that 52.6 mm element at 20 eV instead of 40, arriving later, so the fill window moved from [489.2, 678.3] to [530.7, 719.8] \u2014 the file's own rule (tau = 25% into the measured window; re-measure before changing) applied, measurement at seed 11. Running seed is RANDOM per ; capture count varies run to run \u2014 that is acceptance physics. REQUIRES ion_gym >= v334 (r-z step-gate channel, 2026-08-12). On v333 and earlier the gate's table groups fold into the sin-RF path at their placeholder 1 Hz \u2014 effectively zero \u2014 so the entrance NEVER switches to black: every ion transits, reflects ONCE off the back mirror, and exits; the trajectory view shows twelve single-pass traces and no oscillation. That is the version mismatch speaking, not the design. On >= v334, 4/12 ions trap for the full 3 ms at the ELIT's 246 us period. GATED (2026-08-12): fill in the RED state, entrance switches to BLACK at tau = 536.5 us via the r-z tracer's new step-gate channel (A_red + step(t-tau)*G, exactly parallel to the sin*B channel; G composed from 2-point hold-table groups, one tau per model, longer tables refuse). GATE_E3 lifts endcap_L+E3_L 0 -> 217.1 V; GATE_E2 lifts E2_L 105 -> 140.1 V. tau sits 25% into the measured window [packet fully inside, first return to the entrance] for seed 11 -- the seed is PINNED because tau is ensemble-matched; re-measure the window before changing it. INJECTION v2 (2026-08-12): beamline geometry MEASURED FROM BRIAN'S SLIDE by image analysis, not invented. Calibration: axial 6.785 px/mm from the drawn ELIT's 89.9 mm endcap-to-endcap; radial 17.48 px/mm from the drawn CDMS tube's 3.175 mm bore (cross-check: drawn endcap aperture reads 1.69 vs real 1.5 mm, ~13%). Column, left to right: 5-segment quadrupole platform (segments ~4.05 mm, r0 2.489 mm, ALL at 125 V \u2014 the r-z reduction keeps the DC platform, the RF quadrupole field is not axisymmetric and is absent); tube lenses 125/105/85/10/40/20/0 V at the slide labels (bore r 5.807 mm; the 85 V and 40 V elements are 52.6 mm long); grounded exit wall with r 0.944 mm aperture; 11.6 mm gap; then the ELIT VERBATIM from 's edited spec (paper dimensions, tuned E1 124.4 / E2 148.1 / E3 217.1), entrance in the slide's RED transmission state (E3_L+endcap 0 V, E2_L 105 V), back mirror black. Source: 1.5 mm disc inside the quad platform at 5.3 eV/z (+x); ions FALL from the 125 V platform to ground arriving at ~130 eV/z (source-on-potential rule). RESOLUTION: 0.127 mm/gu for this long-domain demo (the ELIT's 0.127 mm inter-electrode gaps are 1 cell \u2014 bore/gap ~ 55 keeps on-axis fidelity; the trapped-state example keeps 0.0635). In this STATIC state ions transit, reflect once off the back mirror, and exit back out the open gate; trapping requires gating red->black with step tables. SOURCE DISC 0.5 mm (2026-08-12): at 1.5 mm, 11/12 splat on the measured 0.94 mm exit aperture \u2014 geometrically honest for an unfocused parallel beam; a collisionally cooled quad emits ~sub-mm. Column focusing/steering optimization is deliberately NOT done here.",
